    "body": "> What do you mean by incorrect?\r\n\r\nLet's say a window, 'parent' has an auxiliary window 'child'.\r\n\r\n'Child' has 10 forward history entries, all same origin.\r\n\r\n1. 'Parent' grabs all the `NavigationHistoryEntry`s from 'child'.\r\n2. 'Child' performs a 'push' navigation.\r\n3. 'Child' traverses back.\r\n\r\nMy understanding from the spec, is that the `NavigationHistoryEntry`s obtained in step 1 will not 'dispose' in step 2, which is when the history entries actually become invalid. However, they _may_ dispose in step 3, if it results in the previous page returning from the bfcache.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
