    "body": "Thanks Jake, your understanding is correct. We discussed this behavior in some detail in https://github.com/WICG/navigation-api/issues/95#issuecomment-902314407 and some meetings surrounding it. (See also https://github.com/WICG/navigation-api/pull/157#issuecomment-912754893.) I don't think there's a great option here for satisfying both the within-document cases, and the grabbing-someone-else's-`entries()` cases. Since the latter is kind of against the spirit of the navigation API, I think it's OK for the behavior to be suboptimal in that case.\r\n\r\nMaybe we should add some discussion about this, either in the spec or MDN, to make the behavior of `dispose` + bfcache a bit clearer.",
